v6.5 (2026-08-14) = v6.4.1 + the lock/PREFP frontier moved 0.6 -> 0.85.

A spec board gets EITHER the partial preference lock (top 40% by preference
spread pinned to their argmax bay) OR the PREFP 0.85 boost, never both --
stacked they push locked boards over the tardiness edge. Which one it gets was
decided by `_saturation(p) < 0.6`, a bare constant with no measurement behind
it, while P4 sits just above it at 0.796 carrying 19.4% of its objective in
preference regret.

Only instances with bays < 4 and saturation in [0.6, 0.85) change behaviour, so
the gates were run ONLY on those -- every other instance is structurally A/A and
would have diluted the test (4 of 40 train_final, 8 of 40 train).

