Three independent instance sets, no new failure class (the one +84.8% pair sits
on a 113k objective, the high-variance small-objective class, not a `_trivial`
collapse or seed rescue). Expected effect on the preliminary boards: P4 +40.9%
-> +36.7%, P5 +35.3% -> +28.8%; P3 and P6 unchanged because the guard never
fires on P3 (load 0.82) and stands down on P6 (2.86).

Residual risk, recorded: 8 of the 40 enabled instances get worse, some by
8-14%. The pooled medians are -4 to -6% across all three sets and the mechanism
costs exactly nothing where it is inactive (58 of our 86 instances), so the
expected value is clearly positive -- but it is not free.

`peakLoad` is computed at runtime from instance data alone and is
TL-independent, so a hidden finals board decides for itself.

v6.3 (2026-08-13) = v6.2 + mid-run floor promotion.

v6.2's floor covers the paths that returned `_trivial`; the residual tail was
the run that returns its bare seed rescue (P5: 20,111,373, 4+ recorded of 228
draws) because the FINAL checker gate fails on the annealed board with seconds
left, discarding a ~10.6M incumbent. The annealed board exists right after the
portfolio, before the slice spends the tail budget: v6.3 gates a snapshot of
it once (~2-15s of a 480-900s budget, board saved and restored around the
call) and promotes the floor from seed level to annealed level.

Trajectory scope, audited exactly on 08-13: on a checker-feasible incumbent
(~96% of runs) `_gate` returns before touching the engine, and rescue stages
1-2 use no RNG, so the run continues byte-identical to v6.2. Only stage 3
diverges -- `move_block` reseeds `ctx.rng` and `insertGreedy` draws from it
(api.cpp:693), and the board is restored but the RNG is not. That is confined
to runs whose annealed board is infeasible AND unfixable by nudge+retime,
a strict subset of the loss class this mechanism exists to rescue.

Verified deterministically by staging the same recorded catastrophe (final
gate fails): v6.2 returns 20,111,373 (P5) / 45,448,526 (P6); v6.3 returns
10,966,038 / 29,448,742 -- 1.83x / 1.54x. Quality-neutral where it does not
fire: prelim 32 pairs median +0.00% p=0.85, train_final 40 pairs 18W/20L
median +0.03% with no catastrophe on either arm and the sum 0.45% lower.
Expected P5 mean: 11.43M -> ~10.8M (the quantified residual against the
no-failure mean of 10.58M, now mostly covered).

v6.2 (2026-08-12) = v6.1 + the checker-clean floor.

Defect: nothing in a run ever held a board the OFFICIAL checker had accepted.
`_arm_free` spends the whole budget; only when its board fails the checker on a
measure-zero exact-touch artifact does the ladder build a FRESH seed and try to
legalise it, with ~6s left and a checker ladder that needs more. Measured over
every gate ever run: 5 of 228 P5 baseline draws returned `_trivial` at
1,321,314,754 -- 124x the 10.6M median -- and 4 more returned the bare seed at
20,111,373. The P5 MEAN is 45.67M against a 10.64M median, so our true position
there was +491.7%, not +36.6%. It is not P5-specific: train_final 13 drew
4,026,647,139 and 76,951,044 on the SAME seed 7 the grading server uses.

Fix: buy a checker-clean seed board at the start (measured 0.1-0.6s to seed,
0.12-0.38s to gate, under 0.15% of a 600s budget, available 32/32 across 4
boards x 8 seeds) and return it instead of `_trivial`; and never ship a board
the floor already beats, which makes the guarantee a property rather than a
list of enumerated paths. Worth 30x (P6) to 1265x (P3) where it fires.

Verified deterministically, not by a gate -- a 2.3% event is invisible to 48
pairs. tools/floorcheck.py stages the catastrophe by letting `_gate` succeed
exactly once (for the floor) and fail after, which is the state the five
recorded catastrophes were in: 12/12 PASS across 4 boards x 3 entry paths with
every returned board checker-feasible, against 12/12 FAIL for v6.1.

Quality-neutral where it does not fire: train_final 40 pairs 18W/20L median
+0.04% p=0.87; prelim P3-P6 32 pairs median +0.00% p=0.70; P1/P2 smoke
unchanged at the known optima 11,280 / 31,368.

And it fired in its own validation gate: train_final 11 at seed 7 drew
876,467,176 (Z1=65,473, wall 592.6s) on v6.1 and 8,131,553 (Z1=452, wall
587.2s) on v6.2 -- 108x, on one instance, while that gate's sign test read
18W/20L median +0.04%. The median cannot see this; the score can.

